<title>PERU: Group led by Spain's Endesa buys Peru generator.</title>
<headline>Group led by Spain's Endesa buys Peru generator.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium led by Spain's Endesa on Wednesday was awarded a minority holding in state electricity generator Empresa Electrica de Piura, privatization officials said.</p>
<p>Endesa was chosen from five other companies and consortia after it offered to inject $40 million into the company and let the state retain a 59.77 percent stake.</p>
<p>The capital will be used to install an extra 80 megawatts (MW) of capacity within a year.</p>
<p>Empresa Electrica de Piura runs the 54 megawatt Malacas and 12.6 megawatt Verdun thermo-electric centers in the northern department of Piura.</p>
<p>-- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
